so two years ago on October 17th a group  of privileged Villanova students  embarked upon a journey like never  before enrolling into a social justice  documentary class founded by the amazing  Hezekiah Lewis some of us did not know  we were going to Africa especially Ghana  shoutout Caleb abruptly we found  ourselves on set in Ghana filming  footage for a story we had only  partially outlined it took many intense  discussions many possible story lines  and lots of research to come to this  thought-provoking documentary Sankofa  sang Cole for literally means go back  and fetch it you need to go back to your  past in order to understand the present  african-american history did not start  with slavery it interrupted it our film  addresses the loss of African identity  and black males in both Ghana and Africa  in our film we talk about the loss of  African identity in the black male and  how that paralleled disconnect has been  a direct negative result of colonialism  and slavery on behalf of the whole  riptide pictures team we would like to  thank first and foremost God's Way  Anderson and Marquis grant who are  principal characters for allowing us  into their lives and sharing their  stories we would also like to thank our  academic experts Chi Chi a coma and  Amar'e Johnson for giving us helpful  in-store achill insight the stories of  God's Way and marquees represent those  of millions around the world who are  dealing with a historical disconnect  from modes of slavery and colonialism  thank you to the Academy for this  incredible honor to the North family and  the Waterhouse foundation thank you for  your generous donations and your  continued support throughout our process  a huge thank you to father Peter Donahue  and Dean Adele Linda Mayer from  Villanova University for your passion  and willingness to provide resources to  ensure that Sankofa would be seen by  everyone to our professors our mentor  Hezekiah Lewis all we can say is we're  all the good phase we are endlessly  grateful for you when we were in the lab  and so four or five in the morning you  were there with us when we needed  guidance or advice you were there for  all of us through your sacrifice and  dedication this program and storytelling  we are able to share some Coffield on  numerous platforms you gave us the  freedom and responsibility to have  complete say over our phone giving us  the space and confidence to make Sanko  fho thank you for providing student  opportunity on campus for creativity  passion and social justice for pushing  us to make a film that is raw and real  for challenging us in our own personal  and team growth Sankofa would not be  what it is today without you or your  family support especially your wife  leash leash we love you to our families  and friends we are so sorry we all  disappeared for like a year to make this  film there are many late nights many  missed classes and we don't encourage  that missed calls and missed events fire  phone you are all you all were and  continue to be our support system thank  you for all you do we love you from the  bottom of our hearts and I'm almost done  guys so Coco will always be about the  art of storytelling using the art of  film to break down cultural barriers  challenge our own preconceived notions  of the world and share this with others  above all we always want to challenge  perspectives and promote dialogue among  people so that we can begin and continue  to talk about the issues rather than  hide from them in Sankofa we are bold  with our story we believe it is  important to tell the truth within  context and clarity reminding young  black men and women to tell their truth  writing young black men and women that  they are more than what society says  they are we will all keep - we will all  keep pushing to share Sankofa and to  promote advocacy with pure intentions  above all it is meant to invoke everyone  to think about their position in these  systems of oppression that continue to  infest our country today and to act to  make concrete structural change there is  no one-size-fits-all solution to this  problem but being complacent is not the  answer if you are not fighting to end  the problem you are the problem  [Applause]
 

